potency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says banker's rounding. The test expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`, so it failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** The first run (ci-0001) passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch and ran CI again on the updated commit (ci-0002, `0a9452f727`), which also passed.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so the fix is based on the test and the existing docstring. I haven't merged the PR: that needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}